--- job-mix: aarch64, a rehearsal; the number is taken on radon (notes/job-mix.md) ---
qemu-system-aarch64: HVF does not support GICv2 emulation
qemu-runner-aarch64: QEMU refused virt,accel=hvf,gic-version=2,iommu=smmuv3 (its own message is above).
qemu-runner-aarch64: THIS IS NOT YOUR CHANGE. HVF and the GIC version this kernel drives
  are not compatible in this QEMU: kernel/src/drivers/gic.rs speaks GICv2 only, HVF wants
  GICv3. See the BUGS section of notes/interrupts.md, which carries the measurement and
  what a GICv3 driver would be. script/ci-build skips this leg out loud rather than failing;
